      "side": 1,
      "message": "I feel like I\u0027m arguing both sides of an argument here, but adding indexes without knowing _exactly_ the queries that will use them is a recipe for creating a write constrainted database server, and an unmaintainable set of indexes in a hurry. I\u0027d suggest running something like pt-query-digest during a tempest and rally run to get a sense of what queries are running and then make sure they\u0027re covered by sensible indexes.",
