      "side": 1,
      "message": "This really depends on your applications in the cloud; thus, could vary dramatically between clouds. For example, you may run applications that never revoke tokens. So difficult to measure.\n\nissued_before is always queried, so that is an easy one. And user_id and issued_before would be common.  I understand the write issue, but I think this would be a good start.",
